> 
> It's true that genocide is unnecessary.  but why not? 

There is no reason to not genocide a critical(!) or annoying monster
or monster class.

Though we have many choices what to do in our games. And I think you
should make those play decisions that fit best with your experience.

For example, I would rarely wish for a BoH or an AoRefl (there are
exceptions, though) before I saw the upper Sokoban level. I try to
wish for things that I consider necessary in any given state of the
game, or depending on a specific situation.

> Daggers/Knives/Rocks are heavy,

Yes, the more you carry the heavier your equipment. That's the case
with any object in Nethack. Just carry what you think you need most.

> you need to pick them up after you use them,

To pick them up you need to just walk onto that square, not even an
extra turn is required with option pickup-exceptions. If I throw or
drop some item I may want to take it up again if it's useful; that's
Nethack, and I don't see any issue with it.

> and with multishot,
> you occasionally need to care about what's behind the monster.

In those cases you can decide to shoot just a single projectile of
your stack. (That's a standard Nethack feature.)

> 
> If I had a permanent source of Elbereth or levitation, my first wish would
> be for some ?oGenocide to get dragon scales. 

